+printed `#Top` and exited zero. See
+`evidence/kompile-dispatch-mutant2.log` and
+`evidence/kprove-dispatch-mutant2.log`. This mutation changes the program term
+actually selected by the claim; it does not merely edit an external source
+file.
+
+I also authored `evidence/spec-omitted-entry.k` to state the missing composed
+entry theorem. That supplemental prover run was stopped after 120 seconds
+without output and is neither credited to nor charged against the candidate.
+The decisive fact is simpler: this target theorem is absent from the immutable
+submission and was never reported `#Top`.
+
+The formal `StringSeq` domain itself is not narrowed: it inductively denotes
+arbitrary finite lists, each element is an arbitrary finite `IntSeq`, and no
+size bound appears. The failure is result constraint, not source-domain
+coverage.
+
+Stage 4 fails. This defect independently requires a non-legitimate result
+under the benchmark decision boundary.
